.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt HOST 1
.Os Belka
.Sh NAME
.Nm host
.Nd look up names and addresses in the DNS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Ar name | address
.Op Ar server
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks the DNS of
.Ar name ,
and prints what it finds as BIND's host prints it: its addresses, an
alias it is, and the hosts that take its mail.
An
.Ar address
is looked up by its PTR record, under in-addr.arpa.
.Fl t
asks for one record type instead (a, ns, mx, ptr, txt, cname, soa, aaaa
and the rest djbdns knows, or a number);
.Fl a
for any.
The query goes to the resolver
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
names, or to
.Ar server .
.Pp
.Nm
is a shell script over djbdns'
.Xr dnsqr 1 ,
not BIND's host: it has the common forms only.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the name exists; 1 when it does not, or nothing answered.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dig 1 ,
.Xr dnsip 1 ,
.Xr dnsname 1 ,
.Xr dnsqr 1
